{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And gathered.</b> The gladness is gathered to others besides them, and the meaning is that it is removed from them." "<b>The Carmel.</b> For Moab also has a portion in it." "<b>Shall cry out.</b> From the root of תרועה (Leviticus 23:24), from the verbs whose second and last letters are doubled [i.e., roots with a doubled final root letter]." "<b>Hedad.</b> A shout in the winepress to bring out the wine in praise, the opposite of summer and harvest."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:01.625046303Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}